---
import Icon from '../components/ui/Icon.astro';
import Portrait from '../components/patterns/Portrait.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../site.config';
---
<BaseLayout title="About | Ryan Rumana" description="About Ryan Rumana, a Senior AI/ML Engineer who builds applied AI systems, software, and infrastructure.">
  <main id="main-content">
    <section class="section-shell about-hero">
      <div class="container about-hero__grid">
        <div class="about-hero__copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">About me</p>
          <h1>I'm Ryan Rumana.</h1>
          <p>I'm a Senior AI/ML Engineer at Dais, where I lead AI/ML implementation. My projects range from computational theory and applied machine learning to Rust, Kubernetes, and Networking.</p>
          <p>I’m drawn to problems that cross boundaries: models and deployment, algorithms and interfaces, research and reproducibility. Rust, Kubernetes, WebAssembly, and computer vision appear often in my projects because they make those boundaries tangible.</p>
        </div>
        <Portrait />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-shell about-story">
      <div class="container story-grid">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">The through line</p><h2>How I got here.</h2></div>
        <div class="story-copy">
          <p>I studied computer science and engineering at the Colorado School of Mines. That experience taught me to start with the real constraints, test my assumptions, and understand the whole system.</p>
          <p>It is why a cellular-automata question can become a complexity paper and a browser demo. It is why a homelab can grow into a six-node Kubernetes platform. And it is why I care as much about documentation and operations as I do about the interesting core of an implementation.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-shell">
      <div class="container section-grid">
        <div class="principles-heading"><p class="eyebrow">How I work</p><h2>A few durable preferences.</h2></div>
        <div class="principles-grid">
          <article class="principle"><span>01</span><h3>Make the problem legible.</h3><p>Clear framing beats a pile of terminology. I want readers and collaborators to know what matters before they meet the implementation.</p></article>
          <article class="principle"><span>02</span><h3>Own the path to production.</h3><p>A model or service is only useful when it can be built, deployed, observed, and changed without heroics.</p></article>
          <article class="principle"><span>03</span><h3>Show the limits.</h3><p>Benchmarks, proofs, demos, and case studies are strongest when they are specific about what they do not establish.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-shell life-section">
      <div class="container life-band surface-panel">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">Away from work</p><h2>Life outside work.</h2></div>
        <div>
          <p>I was born in Tallahassee, went to college in Colorado, and now live in the Bay Area. In my free time, I train for endurance events, get outside, maintain my Kubernetes cluster, and disappear down whatever technical rabbit hole currently has my attention.</p>
          <div class="life-actions"><a class="text-link" href="/projects/">Explore projects <Icon name="arrow" size={17} /></a><a class="text-link" href={siteConfig.contact.resumeUrl}>Read my resume <Icon name="arrow" size={17} /></a></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-hero__grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.1fr) minmax(280px, 0.55fr); gap: clamp(2rem, 7vw, 7rem); align-items: center; }
  .about-hero__copy { display: grid; gap: 1.15rem; }
  .about-hero__copy > p:not(.eyebrow) { color: var(--color-text-muted); font-size: var(--font-size-lg); }
  .about-story { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-surface-strong) 65%, transparent); border-block: 1px solid var(--color-border-subtle); }
  .story-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(260px, 0.7fr) minmax(0, 1.3fr); gap: clamp(2rem, 7vw, 7rem); }
  .story-grid > div, .story-copy, .principles-heading { display: grid; gap: 1rem; align-content: start; }
  .story-copy { color: var(--color-text-muted); font-size: var(--font-size-lg); }
  .principles-heading { max-width: 42rem; }
  .principles-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); border-block: 1px solid var(--color-border-muted); }
  .principle { display: grid; gap: 0.75rem; align-content: start; padding: 1.5rem; }
  .principle + .principle { border-left: 1px solid var(--color-border-muted); }
  .principle span { color: var(--color-accent-warm); font-family: var(--font-family-mono); font-size: var(--font-size-xs); }
  .principle p { color: var(--color-text-muted); }
  .life-section { padding-top: 0; }
  .life-band { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(280px, 0.9fr); gap: 2rem; padding: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3.5rem); border-top: 3px solid var(--color-accent-pine); }
  .life-band > div { display: grid; gap: 1rem; align-content: center; }
  .life-band > div:last-child { color: var(--color-text-muted); }
  .life-actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 1rem 1.5rem; }
  .text-link { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.4rem; color: var(--color-link); font-weight: 700; }
  @media (max-width: 860px) { .about-hero__grid, .story-grid, .life-band { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .principles-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .principle + .principle { border-left: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border-muted); } }
</style>
